## Symptom
c2c (or shipped binaries) hit glibc compatibility issues on older / certain Linux systems.

## Context
Some hosts report glibc-related failures (binary requires a newer glibc than the system provides, or similar). Exact error surface and which artifact(s) fail still to pin down.

## Repro idea
Confirm with an older baseline image, e.g.:

```bash
docker run --rm -it ubuntu:20.04 bash
# then install/copy the c2c binary and run: c2c --version / c2c doctor / basic send path
```

Ubuntu 20.04 is a good first probe (older glibc than current rolling/LTS build hosts). Also try other targets if needed (e.g. older Debian).

## Expected
Either:
- ship binaries that run on a documented minimum glibc (and CI tests that floor), or
- document minimum glibc clearly and fail with a clear install-time message, or
- provide alternate builds (static / musl / multi-glibc) for older systems.

## Notes
Filed as tracking + repro sketch; fill in concrete error text and affected platforms once confirmed in the Ubuntu 20.04 (or similar) container.